/data/raw/
/data/derived/

# packages/shared-types/src/generated/ is deliberately NOT ignored, and that is a correction rather than
# an oversight. It was ignored, with the comment "built in CI from the OpenAPI document", and two things
# followed that nobody had checked.
#
# `npm run types:check` compares the committed generated types against a fresh generation, so that a route
# cannot change its response shape while the web application keeps compiling against the old one. With the
# file untracked there is nothing to compare, and the script exits 1 saying the file does not exist. The
# CI web job runs that check on a fresh checkout with no generation step before it, so that job could not
# have been passing.
#
# `tsc` cannot compile a fresh clone either: packages/shared-types/src/index.ts imports ./generated/api.js
# and apps/web compiles against it. Found by the Gate 6 fresh clone run.
#
# openapi.json is tracked, so the type file derived from it is tracked too. Generated code that other code
# compiles against belongs in the repository; generated code nothing depends on does not.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini

# Generated by apps/web/scripts/copy-maplibre-worker.mjs. MapLibre's worker plus the shared chunk it
# imports beside it, at a stable path so setWorkerUrl can name it.
apps/web/public/maplibre/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Skill definitions are prose and are safe to track. Settings are not: mcp.json holds bearer tokens
# for the servers it connects to, and one was found there in plain text on 30 August 2026 while it was
# untracked and not yet ignored. A token that reaches a commit object stays in history forever, so the
# directory is excluded rather than the single file, because the next settings file will hold one too.
.kiro/settings/
.agent/tmp/
